cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository (code, materials, preregistrations, or data), please
  cite it. If you refer to the study itself, please cite the preprint under
  `preferred-citation`.
title: >-
  workspace-program: representational and causal studies for "Held but not heeded"
abstract: >-
  Representational (Study 2) and causal (Study 3) arms of a three-study
  preregistered program on whether a language model's verbal acknowledgment that a
  diagnostic category is invented is causally connected to its diagnostic behavior.
  Using a pre-fitted verbalizable-workspace (Jacobian) lens on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct,
  the fictional-status representation is shown to be genuinely held during
  diagnostic generation yet behaviorally inert: projection-ablating it cuts written
  acknowledgments by ~40% while diagnosis remains at 100%. Includes the manuscript,
  three tagged preregistrations, run data, analysis artifacts, and a chain-of-custody
  provenance log. The behavioral arm (Study 1) lives in the sibling repository
  reification-gradient.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Antonio
    family-names: Bernal Suárez
    email: bernalsuarezantonio@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/bernalsuarezantonio-bit/workspace-program'
